QuestGuidance.Register("en",228,{
[7265]="7007212D\n1\tTalk to Mizâdi\tMizâdi is ready to meet with her allies and plan her strategy for Idagâl. You should speak to Mizâdi to begin the meeting.\n2\tListen to the conversation\tMizâdi is speaking with her advisors about the situation in Idagâl. You should listen to the conversation.\n",
[7266]="70059AF7\n1\tTalk to Durin\tDurin has the knowledge now to finish the tale of Mótsog.\n2\tListen to Durin conclude the tale\tDurin has agreed to conclude the tale of Mótsog, for it is not that dwarf's tale alone, but Durin's as well.\n3\tTalk to Durin\tDurin has more to say of the Sunder-battle's aftermath.\n4\tListen to Durin conclude the tale\tDurin has agreed to conclude the tale of Mótsog, for it is not that dwarf's tale alone, but Durin's as well.\n5\tTalk to Durin\tDurin wishes to conclude the tale.\n6\tListen to Durin conclude the tale\tDurin has agreed to conclude the tale of Mótsog, for it is not that dwarf's tale alone, but Durin's as well.\n",
[7267]="7004DA6A\n1\tTalk to King Thorin III\tKing Thorin III is standing before his throne in the Hall Under the Mountain. At King Thorin's request, you have come to attend a great feast and celebration in Erebor.\n2\tAttend the Feast of Durin's Folk with King Thorin\tKing Thorin's feasting table can be found on the landing before his throne in the Hall Under the Mountain. You should attend the Feast of Durin's Folk with King Thorin.\n3\tInspect the seat King Thorin has chosen for you\tYour seat can be found next to Dwalin at the leftmost end of the table. King Thorin has offered you a seat at his table, and you should now inspect it as King Thorin asked.\n4\tTalk to King Thorin III\tKing Thorin is standing beside his table in the Hall Under the Mountain. You have inspected the chair King Thorin chose for you, and you should now speak to King Thorin.\n5\tFind Spakorth, Dréri, and Náth and invite them to the Feast of Durin's Folk\tThe Stout-axes can be found somewhere among the celebrations in the Hall Under the Mountain. King Thorin III has asked you to find Spakorth, Dréri, and Náth in Erebor and offer them an invitation to join the King Under the Mountain at his table.\n6\tInvite Spakorth, Dréri, and Náth to the Feast of Durin's Folk\tSpakorth can be found among the revellers in the Hall Under the Mountain. You have found Spakorth, Dréri, and Náth and should now request that they join King Thorin at his table.\n7\tReturn to your seat at the Feast of Durin's Folk\tYou have summoned the Stout-axes to the Feast of Durin's Folk, and you should now return to your seat at King Thorin's table.\n8\tTalk to Glóin\tGlóin can be found at King Thorin's table in the Hall Under the Mountain. You have returned to King Thorin's table, but just as you were about to take your seat, Glóin tried to get your attention. You should speak to him.\n9\tFind Gimli, Dori, and Nori and send them to the Feast of Durin's Folk\tGimli, Dori, and Nori can be found somewhere in the Hall Under the Mountain. Glóin has asked that you find Gimli, Dori, and Nori and send them to join the Feast of Durin's Folk at King Thorin's table.\n10\tTalk to Gimli\tGimli, Dori, and Nori can be found on the upper level of the Hall Under the Mountain. You have found Gimli, Dori, and Nori and should now urge them to attend the Feast of Durin's Folk at King Thorin's table.\n11\tTalk to King Thorin III\tKing Thorin III can be found at his table in the Hall Under the Mountain. You have found all the missing dwarves and should now return to King Thorin III and attend the Feast of Durin's Folk.\n12\tAwait the arrival of King Thorin's final guest\tKing Thorin III was hoping that one more dwarf would attend the Feast of Durin's Folk, but he is uncertain when or if he will arrive. You should wait with King Thorin III.\n13\tListen to King Thorin III\tKing Thorin III is giving a speech to the Dwarves of Durin's Folk in attendance. You should listen to King Thorin III.\n14\tWitness the arrival of King Thorin's final guest\tFrantic shouting has interrupted King Thorin's speech to the Dwarves of Durin's Folk. You should remain alert and witness the arrival of whoever has been shouting.\n15\tListen to King Thorin III and Nár\tKing Thorin III is speaking to the Dwarves of Durin's Folk and welcoming Nár back to Erebor. You should listen to King Thorin III and Nár.\n16\tTalk to King Thorin III\tKing Thorin III is standing beside his table in the Hall Under the Mountain. All of King Thorin's guests have arrived, and now the feast can begin. You should talk to King Thorin.\n",
[7268]="7003A5BE\n1\tFind the trail of the Boar of Everholt\tThe Boar of Everholt is nearby. The Boar's trail leads to the north, towards the sound of running water.\n2\tFollow the trail of the Boar of Everholt to the north\tFollow the scent of the Boar of Everholt.\n3\tContinue to follow the trail of the Boar of Everholt to the north\tThe Boar of Everholt is very close. You should approach the great creature quietly.\n4\tDefeat the Boar of Everholt\tThe Boar of Everholt is near. You should slay the great beast.\n5\tVerify the Boar of Everholt has succumbed to its wounds\tThe Boar of Everholt has sustained grave injuries and is heading towards the stream. Follow the Boar of Everholt to ensure that you have finally defeated the great beast.\n6\tDo not succumb to the wounds suffered during the battle\tThe fabled Boar of Everholt has finally been defeated. During the battle, you suffered severe wounds and now fight to retain consciousness.\n",
[7269]="70071536\n1\tTalk to Jajax on the dock\tYou have come with Jajax, Rothog, and Belondor to destroy the Narghâk weapons used by the Song.\n2\tIf you tamper with the Narghâk weapons aboard the Ordâkhai ship Kosagháti, you should be able to prevent their further use.\t\n3\tStand by Jajax and decide your next course\tYou have successfully disabled the Narghâk weapons aboard the Ordâkhai ship Kosagháti.\n4\tTalk to Jajax on the Kosagháti\tSomething has happened to the Orc-ship Grishúlvosh. Jajax demands your attention.\n5\tTalk to Rothog beside the burning wreck of the Orc-ship Grishúlvosh\tRothog grieves beside his fallen comrade.\n",
[7270]="70015815\n1\tDefeat Fire-orc summoners (total: 4)\030Defeat Oshadhúr\tYou must defeat the Fire-orc summoners in order to prevent them from summoning enough spirits to destroy the library. If too many spirits are gathered within the library, it will be consumed in an inferno and lost. Once the summoners have been dealth with, you must then face the leader of the Orcs....\n2\tUse the ancient anvil\030Collect Infused Adamant\tUse the ancient forge to emopwer your infused adamant.\n",
[7271]="7004E84F\n1\tTalk to Tuhâl\tTuhâl is nervously waiting to speak to the Jangovar leaders. You should talk to Tuhâl.\n2\tListen to the conversation\tThe Jangovar are conversing. You should listen to the conversation.\n3\tDefeat the Jangovar\tNáin the Slakeless has engaged the Jangovar in battle! You should defeat the Jangovar!\n4\tEscape Utterby with Náin and Tuhâl\tThe dwarves have attacked Utterby! You should follow Náin and escape!\n5\tTalk to Náin\tNáin would like to speak with you. You should talk to Náin.\n",
[7272]="7005843D\n1\tTalk to Bori on the path leading to the threshold of Gundabad\tYou have crossed the lake with Bori, and now he waits to speak with you before you climb to the threshold of Gundabad to meet up with Durin's fighting force.\n2\tPush open the gate to Gorgar's arena\tThe gate to the threshold of Gundabad lies ahead of you, where Gorgar has devised an arena to challenge Prince Durin and his allies. Bori needs your help to push open the gate that lies between you and Durin's fighting force.\n3\tEnter Gorgar's arena and join Durin and his allies\tPrince Durin and his allies stand bravely in the arena of Gorgar the Ruthless on the very threshold of Gundabad.\n4\tRemain on your guard!\tPrince Durin and his allies stand bravely in the arena of Gorgar the Ruthless on the very threshold of Gundabad.\n",
[7273]="7004E755\n1\tTalk to Tuhâl\tThe time has come for Tuhâl of Chayasír to stand before Lord Náin and speak for the Easterling refugees.\n2\tListen to the conversation\tTuhâl is speaking to Lord Náin. You should listen to the conversation.\n3\tTalk to Náin\tYou have been tasked with infiltrating Utterby! You should talk to Náin.\n",
[7274]="7005A800\n1\tTalk to Dáin\tDáin can be found just outside Muru Azog at Azanulbizar. After overcoming Azog's forces at Durin's Stone, Náin Orcsfoe and the Iron-folk have begun their assault on the gates of Khazad-dûm. You should talk to Dáin.\n2\tFollow Dáin and join in the assault on the gates of Khazad-dûm\tDáin can be found at Muru Azog. You have joined in the assault on the gates of Khazad-dûm. You should follow Dáin and aid the soldiers of the Haban’akkâ.\n3\tWitness as Náin confronts Bolg outside Khazad-dûm\tNáin Orcsfoe and the Iron-folk have broken through Azog's defences at Muru Azog. You should aid Náin and the Iron-folk as they approach the gates of Khazad-dûm.\n4\tTalk to Náin\tNáin can be found outside the gates of Khazad-dûm at Muru Azog. Náin Orcsfoe has driven off the coward Bolg, leaving Azog to face the Haban’akkâ. You should talk to Náin.\n5\tConfront Azog\tAzog can be found outside the East-gate of Khazad-dûm. In answer to Náin's taunts, Azog has come out of the shadows of Khazad-dûm. You should confront Azog with Náin and the Iron-folk.\n6\tWitness Náin as he battles against Azog\tNáin and Azog can be found outside the East-gate of Khazad-dûm. Azog has answered Náin's challenge. You should witness the battle between Náin and Azog.\n7\tDefeat Azog's bodyguards\tAzog's bodyguards can be found outside the East-gate of Khazad-dûm. After slaying Náin, Azog has set his bodyguards upon the Iron-folk. You should defeat Azog's bodyguards.\n8\tDefeat Azog\tAzog can be found outside the East-gate of Khazad-dûm. After slaying Náin, Azog hopes to escape the wrath of the Iron-folk. You should aid Dáin and defeat Azog.\n9\tTalk to Dáin\tDáin can be found outside the East-gate of Khazad-dûm. Dáin has slain Azog. You should talk to Dáin.\n10\tWitness as Dáin enters Khazad-dûm\tDáin can be found at the East-gate of Khazad-dûm. After slaying Azog, Dáin has chosen to enter Khazad-dûm. You should watch as Dáin enters Khazad-dûm.\n11\tWait for Dáin\tDáin has walked into Khazad-dûm. You should await Dáin's return.\n12\tTalk to Dáin\tDáin can be found outside the East-gate of Khazad-dûm. After entering Khazad-dûm, Dáin has returned deeply troubled. You should talk to Dáin.\n",
[7275]="700256E0\n1\tSearch the temple for Ferndúr's location\tFerndúr the Virulent has nearly completed his deadly experiments beneath the lost Rhudauran temple. He and his servants must be defeated before his plans come to fruition!\n2\tDefeat Ferndúr the Virulent\tYou have discovered Ferndúr the Virulent, in the central chamber, in the depths of the lost Rhudauran temple. He and his servants must be defeated before his plans come to fruition!\n",
[7276]="70018F14\n1\tSearch the scattered papers for mention of Zurr-thurkh\tPages from the workshop of Melkólf Stonecarver have been scattered all throughout the passage, and you should search them for any mention of Zurr-thurkh, the 'secret road' that might lead into the throne room of Durin.\n2\tSearch the scattered papers for mention of Zurr-thurkh\tPages from the workshop of Melkólf Stonecarver have been scattered all throughout the passage, and you should search them for any mention of Zurr-thurkh, the 'secret road' that might lead into the throne room of Durin.\n",
[7277]="7006B711\n1\tTalk to Silirtas outside Utug-bûr\tGrieving that the Thardúth had their origins as ancient Kintai, Silirtas greatly desires to do her part in sealing them away.\n2\tPlace Narghâk to the left side of the entrance to Utug-bûr (0/3)\tYou and Sigileth have volunteered to place the Narghâk on the left side of the entrance to Utug-bûr.\n3\tPlace Narghâk to the left side of the entrance to Utug-bûr (1/3)\tYou and Sigileth have volunteered to place the Narghâk on the left side of the entrance to Utug-bûr.\n4\tPlace Narghâk to the left side of the entrance to Utug-bûr (2/3)\tYou and Sigileth have volunteered to place the Narghâk on the left side of the entrance to Utug-bûr.\n5\tCheck on the group placing the Narghâk on the other side\tA sense of exhaustion has overcome you once again, as happened earlier when you journeyed within Maurûsh.\n6\tListen to the threatening voice within your mind\tThe ethereal voice speaks threatening words from within the confines of your mind.\n7\tAwaken Silirtas from the enchantment that keeps her from moving\tSilirtas is in grave danger! She must awaken at once!\n8\tPrevent Azagath from inflicting great harm upon Silirtas\tAt the urging of his Thardúth masters, Azagath intends to do great harm to your friends.\n9\tPrevent Azagath from inflicting great harm upon Silirtas\tAt the urging of his Thardúth masters, Azagath intends to do great harm to your friends.\n10\tPrevent Azagath from inflicting great harm upon Silirtas\tAt the urging of his Thardúth masters, Azagath intends to do great harm to your friends.\n11\tStand your ground\tThe Thardúth turn their attention elsewhere in the battle. The sorcerous exhaustion that troubled you has been lifted.\n",
[7278]="700431A5\n1\tApproach Lady Vanyalos\tLady Vanyalos stands between two trees, off the northward road. You have found Lady Vanyalos. You should approach her and see if she can be persuaded to return to Imloth Melui.\n2\tProtect Lady Vanyalos\tLady Vanyalos is wandering on the greensward by the River Anduin. You should protect the Lady Vanyalos and see if you can get her to come to her senses.\n3\tDefeat Tenakrul\030Protect Lady Vanyalos\tFight the Orc captain among the reeds by the River Anduin. Just as Lady Vanyalos fainted, the Orc captain, Tenakrul, came upon you.\n4\tTalk to Lady Vanyalos\tLady Vanyalos stands among the reeds by the River Anduin. Having come to her senses at last, the Lady Vanyalos looks ready to talk to you.\n",
[7279]="7000D3D6\n1\tTalk to Tasgall\tTasgall's hunt has brought the two of you to the slopes of Nád Nathair.\n",
[7280]="70029A57\n1\tTalk to Tomos\tTomos stands nearby. You should speak with Tomos.\n2\tFollow Tomos\tTomos is searching for his wife, Mari. You should follow Tomos through Galtrev.\n3\tFollow Tomos\tTomos is searching for his wife, Mari. You should follow Tomos to Mari's side.\n4\tTry to appease the White Hand overseer\tAn angry White Hand overseer has appeared to make Tomos answer for his crime of missing the day's work. You should speak with the overseer to try to appease him.\n5\tHelp defend the people of Galtrev\tThe half-orc to whom you spoke seems unreasonably angry. You should defend yourself and the townsfolk from the wrath of the servants of Isengard.\n6\tHelp the people of Galtrev\tDefeat the servants of the White Hand.\n7\tTalk to Mari\tMari is in Galtrev. You should speak with Mari.\n",
[7281]="700586FA\n1\tTalk to Derwent Bindweed\tDerwent is pleased to show you around his new home, the town of Stoneheight.\n2\tMeet with some of Derwent's neighbours in Stoneheight\tDerwent doesn't understand why you think Stoneheight has a reputation for danger.\n3\tProtect Derwent and his neighbours from the Orcs\tSomething has happened that has not happened for eight days: Orcs have come to the town of Stoneheight!\n4\tTalk to Derwent Bindweed in Stoneheight\tDerwent Bindweed is frightened, but otherwise unharmed.\n5\tTalk to Derwent Bindweed in Stoneheight\tDerwent Bindweed has made an unpleasant, if not especially surprising, discovery.\n",
[7282]="700147F1\n1\tTalk to Galadriel\tGaladriel is waiting for you in the centre of the garden. You have been summoned to Galadriel's garden in Lothlórien, for she hopes to speak with you.\n2\tLook into the Mirror of Galadriel\tThe Mirror of Galadriel is in the centre of her garden. Galadriel has invited you to gaze into her Mirror to see what you will.\n3\tTalk to Galadriel\tGaladriel is waiting for you in the centre of the garden. You have seen strange sights within the Mirror of Galadriel, including confusing images of Gandalf and a terrible creature: a Balrog, Durin's Bane.\n4\tListen to Galadriel's words concerning your fate\tGaladriel is waiting for you in the centre of the garden. The Lady Galadriel has seen more than the fate of Mithrandir in her Mirror; she has seen some hints of your fate as well.\n5\tTalk to Gwaihir\tGwaihir the Windlord has come to rest in Galadriel's garden. Galadriel has asked you to speak with Gwaihir concerning the fate of Gandalf the Grey.\n",
[7283]="70037DB9\n1\tTalk to Horn in Burg-shápol\tHorn is inside Burg-shápol, the cave in the Everholt where the missing craftsmen might be found.\n2\tTalk to Horn in Burg-shápol\tHorn is in the tunnels of Burg-shápol.\n3\tHorn has stayed behind to delay the approach of the following Orcs, while you search the tunnels of Burg-shápol for the missing craftsmen.\t\n4\tTalk to Nona in Burg-shápol\tYou have found Nona and Corudan in the depths of Burg-shápol.\n5\tTalk to Corudan in Burg-shápol\tCorudan is in the depths of Burg-shápol.\n6\tSurvive the return of the Orcs to Burg-shápol\tMany Orcs have returned to Burg-shápol, and you must defeat them!\n",
[7284]="70015709\n1\tCollect mithril ore-fragments (total: 14)\030Defeat Mine-overseer\tYou must find enough fragments of mithril ore to make proper use of the smelting-forge for the quality. Hopefully, the goblin-slaves have managed to collect enough of the ore for your needs...though they are unlikely to part with it willingly.\n2\tUse the ancient anvil\030Collect Infused Garnet\030Collect Mithril Ore Fragment (total: 14)\tUse the ancient forge and the mitrhil ore-fragments you have collected to empower your infused garnet.\n",
[7285]="7006B58C\n1\tTalk to Rahâzi\tPart of the way back to Iridír, Rahâzi has called for a halt. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n2\tTalk to Rahâzi\tRahâzi and Surdûsha have triumphed over the Ordâkhai, but now a new threat emerges. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n3\tStand your ground against Tatháta and protect the Dumûri warriors\tStand your ground against Tatháta and protect the Dumûri warriors.\n4\tTalk to Rothog the Storm\tRothog the Storm has arrived, and his arrival may have saved you and the Dumûri warriors from Tatháta's wrath.\n5\tTalk to Khôltekh\tKhôltekh has arrived in Ambarûl.\n6\tObserve the meeting of Khôltekh and Rahâzi\tRothog and Khôltekh have arrived in Ambarûl, and they seek to gain permission from its people to carry out the mission they share with you.\n7\tTalk to Rahâzi\tRahâzi waits to speak with you before she departs.\n8\tTalk to Khôltekh\tKhôltekh has some words for you before you continue on to Iridír.\n",
[7286]="700157C3\n1\tCollect stolen tools (total: 4)\030Defeat the morroval-mistress\tYou must defeat the morroval-robbers and recover the tools they have taken from the forge. You must also prevent the fleeing scavengers from escaping the forge, lest they make off with too many important pieces of equipment.\n2\tUse the ancient anvil\030Collect Infused Sapphire\tUse the ancient forge to empower your infused sapphire.\n",
[7287]="70038A26\n1\tSpeak with Grimbold\tGrimbold sits at Théodred's grave at the Fords of Isen. You should speak with Grimbold.\n2\tListen to Grimbold\tGrimbold sits at Théodred's grave at the Fords of Isen. You should speak with Grimbold.\n3\tTell Grimbold the story of Elfhelm's regret\tGrimbold sits at Théodred's grave at the Fords of Isen. You should talk to Grimbold -- tell him the story of Elfhelm's regret. You must select your target and perform the emote.\n4\tTell Grimbold the story of Elfhelm's regret\tGrimbold sits at Théodred's grave at the Fords of Isen. You should talk to Grimbold -- tell him the story of Elfhelm's regret. You must select your target and perform the emote.\n5\tTell Grimbold the story of Hildith's regret\tGrimbold sits at Théodred's grave at the Fords of Isen. You should talk to Grimbold -- tell him the story of Hildith's regret. You must select your target and perform the emote.\n6\tTell Grimbold the story of Hildith's regret\tGrimbold sits at Théodred's grave at the Fords of Isen. You should talk to Grimbold -- tell him the story of Hildith's regret. You must select your target and perform the emote.\n7\tTell Grimbold the story of the king\tGrimbold sits at Théodred's grave at the Fords of Isen. You should talk to Grimbold -- tell him the story of the king's recovery. You must select your target and perform the emote.\n8\tTell Grimbold the story of the king\tGrimbold sits at Théodred's grave at the Fords of Isen. You should talk to Grimbold -- tell him the story of the king's recovery. You must select your target and perform the emote.\n9\tSpeak with Grimbold\tGrimbold is at Théodred's grave at the Fords of Isen. You should speak with Grimbold.\n10\tSpeak with Grimbold\tGrimbold is at the Fords of Isen. You should speak with Grimbold.\n11\tTry to defeat Bosnauk with Grimbold\tThe troll Bosnauk is at the Fords of Isen. You should defeat Bosnauk with Grimbold, if you can.\n12\tObserve the meeting at the fords\tGandalf is at the Fords of Isen. You should speak with Gandalf.\n13\tSpeak with Gandalf\tGandalf is at the Fords of Isen. You should speak with Gandalf.\n",
[7288]="7004D3D8\n1\tPatrol Loeglond.\t\n2\tCheck on the trap\tCheck on the trap.\n3\tTalk to Sírithon\tTalk to Sírithon.\n4\tInvestigate the noises\tInvestigate the noises.\n5\tReturn to the trap\tReturn to the trap.\n6\tTalk to Sírithon\tTalk to Sírithon.\n",
[7289]="70059ACE\n1\tTalk to Durin\tDurin stands in the chamber of Zul-mazal, ready to learn whatever secrets may remain between its walls.\n2\tRemain vigilant while the dwarves consider the chamber\tDurin and the dwarves examine the chamber for clues.\n3\tTalk to Stáli the Hewer\tStáli the Hewer believes his time has come at last.\n4\tObserve the restoration of the mosaic\tThe dwarves believe they have uncovered the key to the mystery of Zul-mazal.\n5\tTalk to Durin\tBósi and Durin have heard the sounds of approaching enemies.\n6\tWitness the completion of the mosaic\tStáli and Fastrith have finished assembling the mosaic.\n7\tTalk to Fastrith\tFastrith has had an idea.\n8\tWitness the completion of the mosaic... again\tFastrith is eager to carry out her idea.\n9\tTalk to Bósi\tBósi, former leader of the Iron Garrison, has warned you that more hobgoblins approach.\n10\tObserve the completed mosaic\tStáli and Fastrith have once again finished assembling the mosaic.\n11\tTalk to Durin\tYou and the dwarves have uncovered the secret of Zul-mazal, and now Durin must decide what should be done.\n",
[7290]="7001AEC6\n1\tTalk to Ianudirel\tSpeak with Ianudirel and fight your way across the bridge to Krul Lugu.\n2\tTalk to Ianudirel to return to Iavassúl.\t\n",
[7291]="7006B54F\n1\tTalk to Sirgon inside the Citadel of Winds\tYou and Sirgon have been escorted to an upper level of the Citadel of Winds.\n2\tTalk to Hármelak inside the tower room\tHármelak and other leaders of the Kindred of the Coins await you in a tower room inside the Citadel of Winds.\n3\tAttend your meeting with the Kindred of the Coins\tWithin a tower room inside the Citadel of Winds, the Kindred of the Coins discuss the days to come.\n4\tTalk to Hármelak inside the tower room\tHármelak and other leaders of the Kindred of the Coins await you in a tower room inside the Citadel of Winds.\n5\tListen to the Kindred discuss the disappearance of Balakhâd\tThe Kindred of the Coins discuss the recent past with you and Sirgon in a tower room in the Citadel of Winds.\n6\tTalk to Belondor inside the tower room\tBelondor wishes to tell you what the Kindred knows concerning Balakhâd's escape from the Citadel of Winds.\n7\tListen to the Kindred discuss the disappearance of Balakhâd\tThe Kindred of the Coins discuss the disappearance of Balakhâd with you and Sirgon in a tower room in the Citadel of Winds.\n8\tTalk to Hármelak inside the tower room\tHármelak wishes to discuss with you the road ahead.\n9\tListen to the Kindred discuss the adventure to come\tThe Kindred of the Coins discuss the mission to pursue Azagath and Nakási.\n10\tTalk to Sirgon in the tower room\tSirgon has volunteered for the dangerous mission to pursue Azagath and Nakási into the wild lands of the east and south.\n11\tListen to the Kindred discuss the adventure to come\tThe Kindred of the Coins discuss the mission to pursue Azagath and Nakási.\n12\tTalk to Hármelak in the tower room\tHármelak wishes to address you before you depart.\n",
[7292]="700215AA\n1\tAccompany Saeradan to confront Gwyllion\tSpeak with Saeradan at Gwyllion's Gate.\n2\tDefeat Gwyllion and her lieutenants\tSeek out Gwyllion at her hut beyond Gwyllion's Gate.\n3\tTalk to Saeradan\tSpeak with Saeradan to return to Echad Saeradan.\n",
[7293]="7002C91B\n1\tTalk to Rothulf\tWynmar, Rothulf, and the other Rohirrim hunters now brace themselves against an onslaught.\n2\tHelp Rothulf rouse Wynmar from his woe\tRothulf and Wynmar are at their camp in Thinglad.\n3\tSee if Wynmar is ready to fight\tRothulf and Wynmar are at their camp in Thinglad.\n4\tDefeat the attacking Orcs\tOrcs are attacking! You must defeat them.\n5\tTalk to Rothulf\tRothulf is at the camp.\n6\tTalk to Wynmar\tWynmar is at his camp.\n7\tSee if Wynmar and Noriel need your help\tNoriel and Wynmar are speaking quietly between themselves.\n8\tAsk Noriel if Wynmar will live\tNoriel is tending to Wynmar's wounds.\n",
[7294]="70071BC6\n1\tWhat is going on?\tIs there a fight in the tavern? You should get closer to see what is going on.\n2\tDefeat the ruffians\tYou found two ruffians beating Sâdikiz as he lay on the floor. You should stop them and defeat the ruffians.\n3\tTalk to Sâdikiz\tYou have defeated the ruffians who were beating Sâdikiz as he lay helpless on the floor. You should talk to the relieved dwarf.\n",
[7295]="70030DE4\n1\tListen to Léofmar's narration\tLéofmar is relaying the tale of his cowardice, for which he believes a curse is his punishment.\n2\tListen to Léofmar's narration\tObserve Léofmar's behaviour.\n3\tFollow Léofmar's narration\tLéofmar is relaying the tale of his cowardice, for which he believes a curse is his punishment.\n4\tListen to Léofmar's narration\tLéofmar is relaying the tale of his cowardice, for which he believes a curse is his punishment.\n",
